This module redistributes the unmodified official Linux release binary. The
release archive is checked against upstream SHA256SUMS when updating this recipe
and pinned by SHA-512 for every build. It does not run the upstream installer:
the system extension owns /usr and zpkg manages binary and service updates.
Runtime configuration, subscription updates, Docker configuration merging,
backups, activation, and removal use the upstream CLI.

The Linux binary includes the Go 1.26.8 runtime (BSD-3-Clause) and these modules:

github.com/pelletier/go-toml/v2 v2.2.4 (MIT)
github.com/spf13/cobra v1.10.2 (Apache-2.0)
github.com/spf13/pflag v1.0.9 (BSD-3-Clause)
gopkg.in/yaml.v3 v3.0.1 (MIT and Apache-2.0)

Their upstream license texts are included under
/usr/share/licenses/oci-mirror-proxy/third-party/, in the go, go-toml, cobra,
pflag, and yaml component directories. The main project's license is LICENSE
in /usr/share/licenses/oci-mirror-proxy/. Module versions and Go module checksums
are recorded in the upstream binary's Go build information and upstream go.sum.
The Go source is available at https://github.com/golang/go/tree/go1.26.8.
The package README documents persistence, automatic Docker integration,
recovery, and removal. Package integration code is covered by the repository
MIT license, included as /usr/share/licenses/oci-mirror-proxy/packaging/LICENSE.
